+.. _cli-config:
+
+Show the Configuration
+----------------------
+
+To see the values that are currently loaded in the app's config, use the
+:func:`config <cli.config_command>` command. The config is printed as JSON.
+
+.. code-block:: console
+
+    $ flask --app hello config
+    {
+      "APPLICATION_ROOT": "/",
+      "DEBUG": false,
+      "SECRET_KEY": "***",
+      "TESTING": false
+    }
+
+The value of any key that contains ``SECRET``, ``PASSWORD``, ``TOKEN``, or
+``KEY`` is replaced with ``"***"``, so the output is safe to share in issues or
+logs. Note that config values are shown as they are, so this is not a way to
+check values set from environment variables at request time.
+
+
+.. _dotenv:
